<title>FRANCE: Legrand 96 profit flat but sees 97 upturn.</title>
<headline>Legrand 96 profit flat but sees 97 upturn.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>  Net						927  vs	     923</p>
<p>  Dividend	 (francs)		   8.15	 up  6.5 pct</p>
<p>  Operating				    1,619  vs	   1,610</p>
<p>  Turnover				    11,502  vs	  11,028</p>
<p>  -- outside France   (percent)	     60  vs		58</p>
<p>NOTE - French electrical equipment maker Legrand said that on a comparable structural and currency basis, turnover was up 2.7 percent. It said the 1996 results were in line with the group's foreasts which took into account the sharp slowdown in its main European markets as well as start-up inefficiencies during the launch phase of major new products.</p>
<p>    An improvement in operating margins seen in the second half of 1996 and the favourable impact of new product lines &quot;should permit the group to start growing profits again&quot; in 1997, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>   (( -- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 ))</p>
</text>
